flowchart TB

LOCAL["`LOCAL WHERE IT ALSO MADE
TECHNICAL SENSE
bge-m3 runs locally on Ollama:
no API cost, documents never leave
the infrastructure
embedding cache in Redis
self-hosted observability stack
MinIO instead of S3 in development
Ollama as the last LLM fallback`"]

NUM["`THE PILLAR HAS A NUMBER — measured
on one real plan, the single roadmap call
cost 84% of the money using only
23% of the tokens
that inversion IS the two-tier argument`"]

TIERS["`SAME SUBJECT, THREE WAYS
everything on Haiku: 0.11 USD
Haiku decides + Nova Lite writes:
0.0125 USD — nine times cheaper
same plan on Sonnet: ~0.79 USD —
sixty-plus times the two-tier cost`"]

TRADE["`THE HONEST TRADE-OFF
the cheap model writes coherent,
structured, good-Portuguese material —
at less than half the volume
the fast model of each family is a
per-deployment knob, no code change`"]

LEDGER["`LEDGER + MONTHLY BUDGET
ledger records the REAL token spend and
the cost of every generation
monthly budget: limit hit → new
generations refused · checked once per
plan, never mid-run — no half-written plans
default 5 USD/month ≈ 400 plans
per teacher`"]

PAID["`WHERE I DID NOT SAVE
PgBouncer · tracing
Argon2 at proper cost · bge-m3
even 24x slower — every one of these
choices has a technical justification`"]

LOCAL --> NUM
NUM --> TIERS --> TRADE
TIERS --> LEDGER
LEDGER -.- PAID

